---
import PageFrame from "../components/PageFrame.astro";
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Logos AI"
  description="Read, search, and study Scripture in the browser, then move into the full Logos AI app for offline access, audio, AI commentary, and deeper workflows."
>
  <PageFrame current="home">
    <main>
      <section class="shell grid gap-10 py-20 lg:grid-cols-[1.15fr_0.95fr] lg:items-center">
        <div class="animate-rise">
          <p class="eyebrow">Read, search, and study Scripture online or offline.</p>
          <h1 class="mt-4 max-w-4xl font-display text-6xl leading-tight text-text md:text-7xl">
            A Bible study app for the browser, desktop, terminal, and private local workflows.
          </h1>
          <p class="mt-6 section-copy">
            Start instantly in the web reader, then move into the full app for offline study, read-aloud, AI
            commentary, and a richer desk for long sessions in Scripture.
          </p>

          <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-4">
            <a href="/try" class="cta-primary">Open web reader</a>
            <a href="/download" class="cta-secondary">Download app</a>
            <a href="https://docs.logos-ai.online" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="cta-secondary">Read docs</a>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-3 text-sm">
            <span class="rounded-full border border-gold/30 bg-gold/10 px-4 py-2 text-gold">Live Bible data</span>
            <span class="rounded-full border border-accent/30 bg-accent/10 px-4 py-2 text-accent">Desktop + CLI + TUI</span>
            <span class="rounded-full border border-border bg-white/5 px-4 py-2 text-muted">Offline-friendly</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="animate-float">
          <div class="surface-card overflow-hidden p-4">
            <div class="rounded-[1.7rem] border border-border/80 bg-bg/60 p-4">
              <div class="mb-4 flex items-center justify-between">
                <div>
                  <div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-muted">Browser Reader</div>
                  <div class="mt-1 font-display text-3xl text-text">John 1</div>
                </div>
                <span class="rounded-full border border-accent/30 bg-accent/10 px-3 py-1 text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent">
                  Live
                </span>
              </div>

              <div class="grid gap-4 lg:grid-cols-[220px_1fr]">
                <div class="rounded-[1.4rem] border border-border bg-surface/70 p-4">
                  <div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-muted">Translations</div>
                  <div class="mt-4 space-y-3">
                    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-gold/45 bg-highlight/70 px-4 py-3">
                      <div class="font-display text-lg text-text">KJV</div>
                      <div class="mt-1 text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-muted">Selected</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-border bg-bg/45 px-4 py-3 text-sm text-text">BSB</div>
                    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-border bg-bg/45 px-4 py-3 text-sm text-text">WEB</div>
                    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-border bg-bg/45 px-4 py-3 text-sm text-text">LSB</div>
                  </div>
                </div>

                <div class="rounded-[1.4rem] border border-border bg-surface/70 p-5">
                  <div class="mb-4 flex items-center justify-between">
                    <div>
                      <div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-muted">Reading Desk</div>
                      <div class="mt-1 font-display text-2xl text-text">Search and navigation</div>
                    </div>
                    <span class="rounded-full border border-gold/35 bg-gold/10 px-3 py-1 text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-gold">
                      Scripture
                    </span>
                  </div>
                  <p class="font-serif text-lg leading-8 text-text">
                    <span class="mr-1 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-gold">1</span>
                    In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with God, and the Word was God.
                    <span class="ml-2 mr-1 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-gold">2</span>
                    The same was in the beginning with God.
                  </p>
                  <div class="mt-6 grid gap-3 md:grid-cols-3">
                    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-border bg-bg/45 px-4 py-3">
                      <div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-muted">Read</div>
                      <div class="mt-2 text-sm text-text">Open a real translation and jump chapter to chapter quickly.</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-border bg-bg/45 px-4 py-3">
                      <div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-muted">Search</div>
                      <div class="mt-2 text-sm text-text">Find verses by phrase, theme, or reference in seconds.</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-border bg-bg/45 px-4 py-3">
                      <div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-muted">Continue</div>
                      <div class="mt-2 text-sm text-text">Move into the full app when you want offline, audio, and deeper study tools.</div>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="shell py-10">
        <div class="surface-card grid gap-6 p-8 lg:grid-cols-[0.9fr_1.1fr] lg:items-start">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">Install Fast</p>
            <h2 class="mt-3 section-title">Use the installer you want.</h2>
            <p class="mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-muted">
              Normal users can grab the native installer from the release page. Power users can go straight to
              Homebrew, Scoop, or the shell bundle without digging through docs first.
            </p>
            <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-4">
              <a
                href="https://github.com/jd4rider/logos-releases/releases/tag/v0.1.4"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noreferrer"
                class="cta-primary"
              >
                Open release
              </a>
              <a href="/download" class="cta-secondary">All download options</a>
              <a href="https://docs.logos-ai.online/setup/voices/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="cta-secondary">
                Kokoro setup
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3">
            <div class="rounded-[1.5rem] border border-border bg-bg/45 p-4">
              <div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-muted">Homebrew</div>
              <code class="mt-3 block overflow-x-auto whitespace-pre-wrap text-xs leading-6 text-gold">
                brew tap jd4rider/logos-ai https://github.com/jd4rider/homebrew-logos-ai
                {"\n"}brew install --cask logos-ai
              </code>
            </div>
            <div class="rounded-[1.5rem] border border-border bg-bg/45 p-4">
              <div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-muted">Scoop</div>
              <code class="mt-3 block overflow-x-auto whitespace-pre-wrap text-xs leading-6 text-gold">
                scoop bucket add logos-ai https://github.com/jd4rider/scoop-logos-ai
                {"\n"}scoop install logos-ai
              </code>
            </div>
            <div class="rounded-[1.5rem] border border-border bg-bg/45 p-4">
              <div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-muted">Shell Bundle</div>
              <code class="mt-3 block overflow-x-auto whitespace-pre-wrap text-xs leading-6 text-gold">
                curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jd4rider/logos-releases/main/install.sh | bash
              </code>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="shell py-14">
        <div class="grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2 xl:grid-cols-4">
          <article class="surface-card p-6">
            <p class="eyebrow">Reading</p>
            <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-3xl text-text">Open Scripture fast</h2>
            <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-7 text-muted">
              Browse translations, books, and chapters in a reader designed to keep you moving instead of burying you
              in tabs.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="surface-card p-6">
            <p class="eyebrow">Search</p>
            <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-3xl text-text">Find passages quickly</h2>
            <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-7 text-muted">
              Search by phrase or keyword, jump straight into a result, and stay in the same reading desk while you
              explore.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="surface-card p-6">
            <p class="eyebrow">Desktop</p>
            <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-3xl text-text">Go deeper in the app</h2>
            <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-7 text-muted">
              The full download adds offline workflows, read-aloud, AI commentary, exports, and a richer environment
              for longer study sessions.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="surface-card p-6">
            <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
            <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-3xl text-text">Use the setup you want</h2>
            <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-7 text-muted">
              Use the hosted experience, bring your own API key, or stay local where the workflow supports it.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="shell py-14">
        <div class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-3">
          <article class="surface-card p-8">
            <p class="eyebrow">Browser</p>
            <h2 class="mt-3 section-title">Start instantly.</h2>
            <p class="mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-muted">
              The web reader is the quickest way into Scripture. Open a translation, search a passage, and get moving
              without installing anything first.
            </p>
            <a href="/try" class="mt-8 inline-flex cta-primary">Launch reader</a>
          </article>

          <article class="surface-card p-8">
            <p class="eyebrow">Desktop</p>
            <h2 class="mt-3 section-title">Study longer.</h2>
            <p class="mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-muted">
              Install the full app when you want offline access, audio, AI help, and a workspace that feels like a
              dedicated study desk instead of a browser tab.
            </p>
            <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
              <a href="/download" class="inline-flex cta-secondary">See downloads</a>
              <a href="https://docs.logos-ai.online/setup/voices/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="inline-flex cta-secondary">
                Voice setup
              </a>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article class="surface-card p-8">
            <p class="eyebrow">Terminal</p>
            <h2 class="mt-3 section-title">Work your way.</h2>
            <p class="mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-muted">
              Logos AI also ships with CLI and TUI surfaces for users who want keyboard-first reading, scripting, or a
              minimal workflow.
            </p>
            <a href="https://docs.logos-ai.online" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="mt-8 inline-flex cta-secondary">Read setup docs</a>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="shell py-14">
        <div class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-[1.05fr_0.95fr]">
          <div class="surface-card p-8">
            <p class="eyebrow">Built for Study</p>
            <h2 class="mt-3 section-title">Keep the text of Scripture central.</h2>
            <p class="mt-5 section-copy">
              Logos AI is designed to make opening, reading, searching, and continuing your study session feel fast and
              natural across browser, desktop, and terminal surfaces.
            </p>
            <div class="mt-8 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
              <div class="rounded-[1.6rem] border border-border bg-bg/45 p-5">
                <div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-muted">Real translations</div>
                <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-text">Use live Bible data in the browser instead of a fake marketing mockup.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="rounded-[1.6rem] border border-border bg-bg/45 p-5">
                <div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-muted">Offline-friendly</div>
                <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-text">Move into the desktop app when you want a stronger offline reading and study flow.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="rounded-[1.6rem] border border-border bg-bg/45 p-5">
                <div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-muted">Audio and AI</div>
                <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-text">Use the browser for reading. Use the full app when you want read-aloud and AI commentary.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="rounded-[1.6rem] border border-border bg-bg/45 p-5">
                <div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-muted">Flexible setup</div>
                <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-text">Hosted access, your own API setup, and local workflows can all fit the same reading and study experience.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="surface-card p-8">
            <p class="eyebrow">FAQ</p>
            <div class="mt-5 space-y-4">
              <div>
                <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-text">Does the browser reader use real Bible data?</h3>
                <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-7 text-muted">Yes. When the public API is configured, the reader uses live API.Bible content in the browser.</p>
              </div>
              <div>
                <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-text">Do I need to install anything first?</h3>
                <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-7 text-muted">No. The web reader is the fastest way to try Logos AI. The desktop app is there when you want the fuller experience.</p>
              </div>
              <div>
                <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-text">Does the app work offline?</h3>
                <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-7 text-muted">The desktop app is the main offline-friendly workflow. The browser reader is aimed at quick access and discovery.</p>
              </div>
              <div>
                <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-text">Is AI required to use it?</h3>
                <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-7 text-muted">No. You can read and search Scripture without AI. AI features are optional and live in the richer app workflows.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="shell py-14">
        <div class="surface-card p-8">
          <div class="flex flex-col gap-6 lg:flex-row lg:items-end lg:justify-between">
            <div>
              <p class="eyebrow">Download</p>
              <h2 class="mt-3 section-title">Open Scripture here. Go deeper in the full app.</h2>
              <p class="mt-5 section-copy">
                Use the browser to start immediately, then install the complete Logos AI app for offline reading,
                read-aloud, AI commentary, and a stronger long-form study environment.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4">
              <a href="/download" class="cta-primary">Open downloads</a>
              <a href="/try" class="cta-secondary">Open web reader</a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>
  </PageFrame>
</SiteLayout>
